      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TALKACHINO (7) can turn the tables after a narrow long neck defeat at Dubbo, where he finished ahead of MICRO MIKKI. His two wins with Jacob Stiff are a solid indicator, and a strong third at Cootamundra adds to his good form. A proven record at 1600m enhances his profile. MARNOO (8) has placed in both runs this campaign and looks ready to strike third-up, with two wins and a placing from five starts at this distance. While NEWS BOUND beat him at Coonabarabran, the weight relief gives MARNOO a chance to turn the tables. MICRO MIKKI (1) has shown better recent form than his last fourth suggests, facing trouble at Dubbo but benefiting from a strong rider in Clayton Gallagher. He carries top weight but handles wet ground well. NEWS BOUND (6) arrives in winning form after two BM66 victories, though she needs to prove her ability at 1600m. MACLEAY (5) claim helps again in a weaker race.",
